  "description": "FastG (\"Fast Geometry\"): a small, fast geometry library for games and real-time applications: points, vectors, rectangles, circles, ellipses, triangles, polygons, rays, planes, spheres, cubes, AABBs, capsules, cylinders, and N-dimensional vectors.\n\nEvery shape is an immutable value type (readonly struct), so building one per frame or running thousands of intersection tests in a tight loop allocates nothing and adds no GC pressure. Shapes carry value equality (==, Equals, GetHashCode) and work correctly as dictionary keys. Includes intersection and containment tests, distances, area / volume / perimeter, and arithmetic operators.\n\nCoordinates are stored as float — the library trades precision for speed and is not intended for CAD or scientific computing. AARectangle, Cube, and AABB are axis-aligned (no rotation).\n\nMIT licensed.",
